  "sn48.39:6.1": "Experience depends on the collision of disparate elements, whose friction or “resistance” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>paṭigha</i>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn15/en/sujato#20.4'>DN 15:20.4</a>) sparks the light of consciousness. Hence consciousness, like fire, is beautiful but also burning (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn35.28/en/sujato'>SN 35.28</a>). | This simile is also found at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn140/en/sujato#19.13'>MN 140:19.13</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn12.62/en/sujato#4.1'>SN 12.62:4.1</a>, and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn36.10/en/sujato#1.10'>SN 36.10:1.10</a>. ",
  "sn48.39:6.2": "",
  "sn48.39:6.3": "",
  "sn48.39:6.4": "Text switches from “arisen” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>uppanna</i>) to “arises” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>uppajjati</i>). ",
